{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Only take heed to yourself.</b> Even though I have said that you are worthy of being accounted wise in the eyes of the nations, take heed to yourself from the opinions of those errants who deny the existence of Elohim blessed be He, and His power, and His providence — and who think to bring rational proofs for all of this." "<b>Lest you forget the things that your eyes saw.</b> And the reason I have warned you most strongly to guard against this is that there is cause to fear lest you forget what your physical eyes saw at Sinai, and your intellectual eyes as well in the explanation of the Torah, through which you were shown to know the opposite of their opinions by means of rational demonstrations." "<b>And you shall make them known to your children.</b> Your children who were not present then — you shall make known by means of rational demonstrations."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:20:22.892960265Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}